    <string name="fact_card_title">Did you know</string>
    <string name="fact_source_label">Source: %1$s</string>
    <string name="fact_view_source">View the source</string>
    <string name="fact_no_single_normal">Only about one person in six has a median cycle of 28 days. There is no single “normal” length.</string>
    <string name="fact_most_cycles_in_range">About nine people in ten have cycles between 21 and 35 days.</string>
    <string name="fact_variation_is_common">Nearly a third of people see their cycle length vary by six days or more from one cycle to the next.</string>
    <string name="fact_variation_by_age">Cycle regularity changes with age: on average it is most stable between 35 and 39.</string>
    <string name="fact_mean_length">The average cycle lasts 28.7 days, and nine cycles in ten last between 22 and 38 days.</string>
    <string name="fact_same_person_varies">Within the same person, cycle length varies by 2.6 days on average from one cycle to the next.</string>
    <string name="fact_irregular_definition">A cycle is described as irregular when the interval is shorter than 21 days or longer than 35 days.</string>
    <string name="fact_long_cycles_common">About one person in twelve has cycles longer than 35 days.</string>
    <string name="fact_short_cycles_rare">Cycles shorter than 21 days are rare: they affect fewer than one person in five hundred.</string>
    <string name="fact_ovulation_not_day_14">Ovulation happens on day fourteen in only about one cycle in eight.</string>
    <string name="fact_luteal_varies">The luteal phase does not always last fourteen days: lengths of fourteen and fifteen days each account for about one cycle in six.</string>
    <string name="fact_cycles_shorten_with_age">Cycles of 27 days are about twice as common after 40 as between 18 and 24.</string>
    <string name="fact_quarter_very_regular">A quarter of people have very stable cycles, varying by a day and a half or less.</string>
    <string name="fact_variation_after_50">After 50, cycle variability is on average nearly three times higher than between 35 and 39.</string>
    <string name="fact_median_iqr">The median cycle lasts 28 days, and half of all cycles last between 26 and 30 days.</string>
    <string name="fact_variation_late_forties">Between 45 and 49, cycle length varies more on average than between 25 and 29.</string>
    <string name="fact_large_cohort_mean">Across more than 600,000 cycles studied, the observed average length is 29.3 days.</string>
    <string name="fact_period_duration">A period usually lasts between 2 and 7 days, most often around 5 days.</string>
    <string name="fact_blood_volume">The volume of blood lost during a period is usually between 20 and 90 millilitres.</string>
    <string name="fact_menarche_age">A first period usually arrives around age 12, sometimes earlier or later.</string>
    <string name="fact_menopause_age">Menopause usually happens between the mid-forties and the mid-fifties.</string>
    <string name="fact_ovulation_counts_backwards">Ovulation happens about 12 to 16 days before the next period starts, not on a fixed day of the cycle.</string>
    <string name="fact_not_shameful">The WHO calls for environments where menstruation is seen as normal and healthy, not as a source of shame.</string>
    <string name="fact_health_not_hygiene">The WHO points out that menstruation is a matter of health, not hygiene.</string>
